<title>UK: Natwest Markets backs William Cook forecast.</title>
<headline>Natwest Markets backs William Cook forecast.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Natwest Markets Plc, adviser to takeover target William Cook, said on Friday it stood by the accuracy of a profit forecast issued by the company, which was questioned by predator Triplex Lloyd.</p>
<p>Natwest, acting as financial adviser to Williams, said it was &quot;satisfied that...the profit forecast has been properly prepared by the directors of William Cook with scrupulous care and objectivity. Comments to the contrary should be disregarded.&quot;</p>
<p>Triplex had said the forecast was &quot;implausible,&quot; representing an unsustainable profitability level.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
